  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "text": "Cook onions slowly with butter and oil in covered saucepan for 15 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Uncover, raise heat to moderate, and stir in salt and sugar. Cook 15 - 20 minutes, stirring frequently, until onions have turned an even, deep, golden brown."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "In another saucepan, bring beef bouillon to a boil. Sprinkle flour into onions and stir for 3 minutes."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "Off heat, blend in 1/2 of boiling bouillon. When well blended, add remaining broth. Add wine and season to taste. Simmer partially covered for 30 - 40 minutes. Correct seasoning. Can set aside, then reheat. to simmer."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "JUST BEFORE SERVING, stir in optional cognac. Place cheesy croutes in tureen or bowls, pour in soup. CROUTES"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "text": "Cut bread into 12 - 16 slices, 3/4 - 1\" thick. Place in single layer and cook at 325 for 1/2 hour."
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "text": "Halfway through baking, baste slices with olive oil."
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "text": "Towards the end, add Gruyere to slices, and cook until cheese is just melted."
    }
  ],
